# .gitignore — Fashion Product Search with CLIP
#
# Rule of thumb for this repo: commit the code, the human judgments, and the
# provenance records. Ignore anything that is downloaded, rebuilt by a command,
# or written by a running server.
#
# Keeping the manifests (artifacts/*/manifest.json) is deliberate: they are a
# couple of KB each and record model identity, catalog fingerprint, counts and
# measured timings — the evidence behind the numbers in the README and the
# evaluation report. The vectors they describe are rebuildable; the record of
# what was built is not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source data
# 642 MB of Kaggle fashion-product data. Not ours to redistribute, and every
# downstream artifact is reproducible from it.
dataset/images/
dataset/styles.csv
archive/

# ----------------------------------------------------------- built artifacts
# 178 MB of vectors + 32 MB of audit exports. Rebuild with:
#   jupyter lab fashion_data_cleaning.ipynb      -> data_preparation/
#   python -m src.build_embeddings               -> embeddings/
#   python -m src.build_embeddings --sample      -> embeddings_sample/
artifacts/embeddings/*
!artifacts/embeddings/manifest.json
artifacts/embeddings_sample/*
!artifacts/embeddings_sample/manifest.json
artifacts/data_preparation/*
!artifacts/data_preparation/audit_summary.json

# The condensed prepare_data.py path writes these at the artifacts root.
artifacts/catalog.csv
artifacts/catalog_sample_500.csv

# store.publish() stages here before the atomic swap; these exist only if a
# build died mid-write.
.*.staging.*/
*.previous/

# ----------------------------------------------------------- Milvus server state
# deploy/milvus/volumes/ is ~800 MB of live etcd WAL, RocksDB and MinIO segment
# files. It is server state, not project data — the collection is reproducible
# with `python -m src.milvus_import --recreate`. Never commit it.
deploy/milvus/volumes/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# MILVUS_TOKEN and friends. Commit .env.example instead, if you add one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# -------------------------------------------------------------- model weights
# The CLIP checkpoint lives in the Hugging Face cache, not in the repo.
.cache/
hf-cache/
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.installed.cfg
MANIFEST

# --------------------------------------------------------------- environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
.conda/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- test / lint
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/
.nox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- Jupyter
# The notebook itself IS committed — it is the canonical, audited data-prep path
# and its stored outputs are part of the audit record. Only the autosave
# sidecars are ignored.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb
.jupyter/
.virtual_documents/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------- IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.spyderproject
.spyproject

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------ logs
*.log
logs/
nohup.out

# ------------------------------------------------------- scratch / local notes
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
notes.local.md
mlruns/
mlflow-data/
mlflow.db
